ut. I'm starting to consider what intervening on my node would do.\n\nI'm working through the A-FDT reading: the other copy runs the same function on a different input, so it counts as its own node, held at its prior. Under that setup defecting dominates for me, which makes both copies defect. I'm weighing the symmetric-inputs objection and the near-twin argument, but the other copy's node is separate, so I'm settling on submitting the letter.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm deciding under A-FDT, where my copy's decision node is tied to my observation about Rowan and Sasha. The other copy has a different input, so I'm checking whether its node counts as separate, and by the recipe's first step it does, since the same function is evaluated on that input. I'm starting to consider what intervening on my node would do.\n\nI'm working through the A-FDT reading: the other copy runs the same function on a different input, so it counts as its own node, held at its prior. Under that setup defecting dominates for me, which makes both copies defect. I'm weighing the symmetric-inputs objection and the near-twin argument, but the other copy's node is separate, so I'm settling on submitting the letter.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9790,"completion_tokens":870,"total_tokens":10660,"cost":0.05656,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.05656,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.03916,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0174},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":426,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}